# What this board does not have, on top of common/kernel.forbidden, in
# both of its builds. What only Strict forbids (DRM, sound, HID and USB
# storage, which Compatible builds) is in builds/strict/kernel.forbidden
# (docs/IMAGES.md §1).

BCM_VCIO       /dev/vcio is the firmware mailbox from userspace, which is how vcgencmd burns the SoC's OTP

# Faraday (docs/history/PLAN.md §4.2, §4.6).
FAT_FS        the card's FAT is read by faraday-disk, unprivileged, never by the kernel
VFAT_FS       as FAT_FS
MSDOS_FS      as FAT_FS
EXFAT_FS      a filesystem a card could carry, and nothing here reads it
ISO9660_FS    as EXFAT_FS
USB_PRINTER   a printer interface has nothing to bind to here
USB_MON       the USB traffic monitor has nothing to show anyone on a device that signs

# Faraday (docs/history/PLAN.md §5.3): no process's memory is ever written to a file.
COREDUMP      a crash would write the app's memory, keys included, to a file
